## English

### 1. Who we are

**Alshy** is a Kazakh-language party and learning game app (quiz, words, math, alphabet, battle, Who’s the Spy?, Mafia). Android package: `kz.alshy.games`.

Operator: the app developer. Contact: [https://github.com/makosh24/alshyApp/issues](https://github.com/makosh24/alshyApp/issues).

### 2. Summary

We do **not** create accounts, show ads, use analytics SDKs, or send personal data to our own servers. Game data stays on the device. Multiplayer works only on the **same local Wi-Fi**, when you host or join.

### 3. Data we process

**On-device only (not sent to the developer):**

- optional player name for LAN lobbies;
- “tutorial already seen” flags;
- custom words and optional microphone recordings (“new words” mode);
- a local copy of an audio file you pick;
- any leftover campaign save data stored by the app.

**On the local network (only if you start or join a game):**

- player name, round state, moves, and scores between devices and a TV browser on the same Wi-Fi;
- local spectator page at `http://alshy.local:8080`.

We do not collect email, phone numbers, precise location, payment data, or advertising IDs.

### 4. Permissions

- **Microphone** — optional, only to record a custom word. Deny it and built-in words still work. Recordings stay on the device.
- **Internet / Wi-Fi / multicast** — LAN game discovery and the local `alshy.local` page. No cloud account server.
- **File picker** — attach your own audio to a custom word (copied into app storage).

Text-to-speech uses the device’s system engine.

### 5. Third parties

No ads, payments, or analytics SDKs. If you open WhatsApp or another app yourself to share a local URL, that service’s policy applies. We do not receive a copy of the message.

### 6. Children

The app includes kids’ modes. We do not collect children’s personal data, build profiles, or show ads.

### 7. Retention and deletion

Data remains on the device until you uninstall the app or clear its storage. We do not keep a copy on our servers, so there is nothing for us to delete remotely.

### 8. Changes

If this policy changes, we will update the date on this page.
